  t["Consumo eléctrico"] = "Power consumption";
  t["Contamos los vértices de grado impar: hay <strong>"] = "We count the vertices of odd degree: there are <strong>";
  t["Contando lo que ya viene de camino, nadie pide dos veces lo mismo y el látigo se amansa."] = "Counting what is already on its way, nobody orders the same thing twice and the whip is tamed.";
  t["Contando todo, «gato» y «gata» salen a <strong>0,149</strong> de parecido, que es absurdo: son casi la misma palabra. El culpable es el artículo. Quitando las palabras vacías suben a <strong>0,632</strong>, y «nino»·«nina» pasa de 0,15 a <strong>0,75</strong>. La moraleja es general: <strong>una palabra que aparece en todas partes no distingue nada</strong>."] = "Counting everything, “gato” and “gata” come out at <strong>0.149</strong> of likeness, which is absurd: they are almost the same word. The culprit is the article. Removing the stop words they rise to <strong>0.632</strong>, and “nino”·“nina” goes from 0.15 to <strong>0.75</strong>. The moral is general: <strong>a word that appears everywhere distinguishes nothing</strong>.";
  t["Contar $n$ copias con espejo"] = "Counting $n$ copies with a mirror";
